THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
======================

This repository vendors one piece of third-party source, recorded immediately
below, and ships one compiled third-party-bearing artifact:
dist/ValheimProfileSync.exe is a statically linked Go binary that embeds the Go
standard library and the modules listed under GO DEPENDENCIES below. Their
notices are reproduced there, as their licenses require of a binary
distribution.

Octicons (GitHub mark)
  Upstream:  https://github.com/primer/octicons
  License:   MIT
  Copyright: (c) GitHub, Inc.
  Role:      The mark-github-16 glyph is inlined in internal/app/server.go as
             the icon on the source-code link the player-facing pages carry,
             which is this program's AGPL section 13 source offer. It is inlined
             rather than served as an image file so that fill:currentColor
             matches it to the surrounding navigation.
  Note:      The Invertocat mark is a GitHub trademark. It is used here only to
             link to a repository hosted on GitHub, which GitHub's brand
             guidelines permit. A deployment that moves its source elsewhere
             should set PORTAL_SOURCE_URL and replace the glyph.

The runtime components below are obtained separately by the operator. They keep
their own licenses; the AGPL covers only the code in this repository.

valheim-server-docker
  Upstream:  https://github.com/lloesche/valheim-server-docker
  License:   Apache License 2.0
  Role:      Builds and runs the container that hosts the Valheim dedicated
             server. The agent's start, stop, and build operations drive it
             through docker compose.
  Note:      No copy of it is distributed here. VALHEIM_SERVER_DOCKER_DIR names
             the operator's own checkout, which the host operation scripts run
             docker compose against. If you redistribute a modified copy of
             valheim-server-docker itself, Apache-2.0 section 4 requires that
             you retain its LICENSE, carry its NOTICE, and state the changes
             you made.

BepInEx
  Upstream:  https://github.com/BepInEx/BepInEx
  License:   LGPL-2.1
  Role:      Mod loader bootstrapped into the client profile and used to load
             the map export plugin.

Thunderstore packages
  Role:      Profile definitions reference mod packages such as ValheimVR,
             EpicLoot, and Backpacks by exact version and SHA-256.
  Note:      Each package carries its own license and its own terms about
             repackaging. Redistribution of these payloads is UNRESOLVED and
             must be settled before this portal serves the public. See
             docs/public-distribution.md.

Valheim and its assemblies
  Publisher: Iron Gate AB
  Role:      The map source exporter is compiled against the server's own
             managed assemblies (assembly_valheim.dll, UnityEngine.dll, and
             others) that are present on the host.
  Note:      No Valheim game file, Unity runtime file, or server binary is
             contained in this repository, and the build refuses to package
             them. This is NOT the same as saying none is distributed: a
             running portal serves profile definitions whose ValheimVR flat
             companion and VR runtime artifacts contain Unity XR runtime
             assemblies, Microsoft's non-redistributable debug CRT
             (ucrtbased.dll), and paid Unity Asset Store libraries
             (final_ik.dll, amplify_occlusion.dll). Those artifacts are built
             and supplied by the operator, are deliberately absent from this
             repository, and MUST NOT be redistributed. Serving them to
             players is the UNRESOLVED question recorded under Thunderstore
             packages above; see docs/public-distribution.md and
             ../boilerplate/mods/valheimvr/README.md.


